From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: a refused texture upload backs off before it is tried again (waveydude's 0919, EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF), off by default

What: a texture upload that finds no staging buffer, or whose decode the pool refused
(EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT's refusal included), goes to UploadLater: the image stays CPU-modified and
the next draw that samples it tries again. Under a long shortage that is every use, each one a
refused staging request on the GPU thread.

With EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF=1 (exact "1", read once) UploadLater counts the refusals in a row and
RefreshContents skips the image until frame_tick passes upload_retry_frame: 8, 16, 32, 64, then
128 frames (upload_retry.h, BackoffFrames). A guest write to the image (the two places that mark it
CPU-modified) and an upload that goes through reset the count and the wait. At the
EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES-th refusal in a row (unset: 8, as in his 0919; "0": no limit) the image
is given up: CpuModified cleared, drawn with what it holds until the guest writes it again, one
LOG_ERROR line; with EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS=1 a bad_alloc is thrown instead.

Do not use this on its own: an image given up before its first upload is black until the game
writes it again. 0665 (his 0924) takes the limit away by default; use the two together.

Changed from his: the switch (his 0919 has none: always on); the helpers are a core header
(video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h, from his headless/upload_retry.h of 0924) so the core
needs nothing of the wrapper; his UploadInChunks change ("return false" for "UploadLater; break")
is left out: a refused chunk still goes to UploadLater, and the upload_retry_frame test after it
already tells a refused upload from one that went through; his unused KeepContentsFallback
declaration is left out.

Off: two image fields that stay 0 (16 bytes per image with padding), two stores of 0 where the guest writes an
image, one compare of a 0 frame per refresh of a CPU-modified image, one test of a static bool per
refusal; no waits, no limit, no line. Not in the kept-store stamp.

Origin and credit: waveydude, patch 0919 ("Back off repeated texture upload refusals"), commit
792612f; BackoffFrames, GiveUp and NextFailCount from his headless/upload_retry.h (commit 2ca0fdb).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h
index ab11361..37a62e4 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/image_base.h
@@ -152,6 +152,10 @@ struct ImageBase {
     /// (raised when an alias's tick is set or an alias is added): SynchronizeAliases has nothing
     /// to do while it is not newer. Never read with the switch off.
     u64 newest_alias_tick = 0;
+    /// EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF (waveydude's 0919): the frame before which a refused upload is not
+    /// tried again, and the refusals in a row. Both stay 0 with the switch off.
+    u64 upload_retry_frame = 0;
+    u32 upload_fail_count = 0;
     size_t lru_index = SIZE_MAX;
 
     /// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE / _COLD (Fritchii c98e63520a): the frame the GPU last wrote the
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index e60ce70..c54e7d3 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #include "video_core/texture_cache/image_view_base.h"
 #include "video_core/texture_cache/samples_helper.h"
 #include "video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h"
+#include "video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h"
 #include "video_core/texture_cache/util.h"
 #include "video_core/nx2.h"
 #include "video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h"
@@ -241,6 +242,14 @@ constexpr u64 KeepRemadeWindow = 600;
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF=1 (exact "1", read once; waveydude's 0919): a refused texture upload
+/// (UploadLater) is not tried again at every use but after a back-off that grows to 128 frames,
+/// with an optional give-up limit (EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES, upload_retry.h). Off: as before.
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool UploadBackoff() {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 /// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE=1 (off unless set; Fritchii c98e63520a + 07b38b3caf, EXP43=3 of
 /// 1735a6fd13): a render target a clear overwrites whole, which drifted a little off one or more
 /// images of its own single-level, single-layer 2D shape (Ocarina of Time's bump-allocated
@@ -3528,6 +3537,9 @@ void TextureCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr cpu_addr, size_t size) {
             MarkLayersWritten(image, cpu_addr, size);
             return;
         }
+        // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF: the guest wrote it again, so the next use tries at once.
+        image.upload_fail_count = 0;
+        image.upload_retry_frame = 0;
         if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::CpuModified)) {
             return;
         }
@@ -3682,6 +3694,8 @@ void TextureCache<P>::UnmapGPUMemory(size_t as_id, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, size_t siz
         Image& image = slot_images[id];
         if (False(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::CpuModified)) {
             image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::CpuModified;
+            image.upload_fail_count = 0; // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF: new contents, no wait
+            image.upload_retry_frame = 0;
             if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Tracked)) {
                 UntrackImage(image, id);
             }
@@ -4443,6 +4457,11 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RefreshContents(Image& image, ImageId image_id) {
         // Only upload modified images
         return;
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF (UploadLater): a refused upload waits out its back-off; the image
+    // keeps what it holds until then. Never true with the switch off (the frame stays 0).
+    if (image.upload_retry_frame > frame_tick) {
+        return;
+    }
     VideoCommon::Nx2Profile::Scope profile_scope{VideoCommon::Nx2Profile::Zone::TextureUpload};
     HitchTrace::Op upload_trace{HitchTrace::Kind::ImageUpload, image.guest_size_bytes,
                                 HitchTraceDesc(image.info, image.gpu_addr)};
@@ -4555,6 +4574,9 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RefreshContents(Image& image, ImageId image_id) {
     ++images_uploaded;
     uploaded_bytes += image.guest_size_bytes;
     largest_upload = (std::max<u64>)(largest_upload, image.guest_size_bytes);
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF: UploadLater sets the frame again when this upload is refused, so
+    // a frame still 0 below means the upload went through and the refusal count starts over.
+    image.upload_retry_frame = 0;
     try {
         if (!UploadInChunks(image)) {
             if (auto staging = UploadStagingNow(runtime, MapSizeBytes(image))) {
@@ -4566,11 +4588,16 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RefreshContents(Image& image, ImageId image_id) {
                 if (refused) {
                     UploadLater(image);
                 } else {
+                    image.upload_fail_count = 0;
                     runtime.InsertUploadMemoryBarrier();
                 }
             } else if (!UploadInChunks(image, 0)) {
                 UploadLater(image);
+            } else if (image.upload_retry_frame == 0) {
+                image.upload_fail_count = 0;
             }
+        } else if (image.upload_retry_frame == 0) {
+            image.upload_fail_count = 0;
         }
     } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
         // No memory for one image's unswizzle or conversion scratch (tens of MiB in one piece, on
@@ -4615,6 +4642,29 @@ void TextureCache<P>::UploadLater(Image& image) {
                             "its upload waits for its next use",
                     image.gpu_addr, MapSizeBytes(image), times);
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF=1 (exact "1"; waveydude's 0919): the next try waits 8, 16, 32, 64,
+    // then 128 frames (RefreshContents skips the image until then), and with
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES=<n> the image is given up at its n-th refusal in a row: drawn
+    // with what it holds until the guest writes it again. Off: as before (no wait, no limit).
+    if (UploadBackoff()) {
+        image.upload_fail_count = UploadRetry::NextFailCount(image.upload_fail_count);
+        static const u32 max_retries =
+            UploadRetry::ReadMaxRetries(std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES"), 8);
+        if (UploadRetry::GiveUp(image.upload_fail_count, max_retries)) {
+            if (const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS"); value && value[0] == '1') {
+                throw std::bad_alloc{};
+            }
+            LOG_ERROR(HW_GPU, "Repeated upload failures for image at {:#x}: keeping existing contents",
+                      image.gpu_addr);
+            image.flags &= ~ImageFlagBits::CpuModified;
+            runtime.TransitionImageLayout(image);
+            VideoCommon::Nx2FastDraw::Break(VideoCommon::Nx2FastDraw::Reason::Invalidation);
+            image.upload_fail_count = 0;
+            image.upload_retry_frame = 0;
+            return;
+        }
+        image.upload_retry_frame = frame_tick + UploadRetry::BackoffFrames(image.upload_fail_count);
+    }
     image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::CpuModified;
     runtime.TransitionImageLayout(image);
     // EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW: the next draw that samples it uploads it, as without fast draws.
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ca557b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2026 Eden Emulator Project
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+
+// EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF (texture_cache.h UploadLater): when a texture upload that found no
+// memory is tried again, and when it is given up. From waveydude's 0919 and his
+// headless/upload_retry.h (0924), here in the core so the texture cache needs nothing of the
+// wrapper's.
+#pragma once
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdlib>
+
+namespace VideoCommon::UploadRetry {
+
+constexpr std::uint64_t MaxBackoffFrames = 128;
+
+/// Frames to wait after the `fail_count`-th refusal in a row (1 for the first): 8, 16, 32, 64,
+/// then 128 for every one after.
+constexpr std::uint64_t BackoffFrames(std::uint32_t fail_count) {
+    const std::uint32_t shift = std::min<std::uint32_t>(fail_count, 5) + 2;
+    return std::min<std::uint64_t>(std::uint64_t{1} << shift, MaxBackoffFrames);
+}
+
+/// EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES as text: the refusals in a row after which the image is given up.
+/// No text: `unset`. "0", or text that does not start with a digit: 0, never given up.
+inline std::uint32_t ReadMaxRetries(const char* text, std::uint32_t unset) {
+    if (text == nullptr) {
+        return unset;
+    }
+    if (text[0] < '0' || text[0] > '9') {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    const unsigned long value = std::strtoul(text, nullptr, 10);
+    return value > 0xffffffffUL ? 0xffffffffU : static_cast<std::uint32_t>(value);
+}
+
+/// Whether the image is given up at its `fail_count`-th refusal in a row.
+constexpr bool GiveUp(std::uint32_t fail_count, std::uint32_t max_retries) {
+    return max_retries != 0 && fail_count >= max_retries;
+}
+
+/// The count after one more refusal: it stops at its top instead of wrapping to 0, which would
+/// start the short waits again.
+constexpr std::uint32_t NextFailCount(std::uint32_t fail_count) {
+    return fail_count == 0xffffffffU ? fail_count : fail_count + 1;
+}
+
+} // namespace VideoCommon::UploadRetry
